<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Vincent Huang</title><link>https://vh-x.github.io/</link><description>Recent content on Vincent Huang</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 18 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://vh-x.github.io/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Keep Your Terminal Setup in Sync with Git &amp; Stow</title><link>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/keep-your-terminal-setup-in-sync-with-git-stow/</link><pubDate>Thu, 18 Jul 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/keep-your-terminal-setup-in-sync-with-git-stow/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Every developer has been there: you spend time getting your terminal just right — your prompt, your aliases, your editor config — and then you set up a new machine and have to do it all over again. Or worse, you make a tweak on one machine and forget to replicate it on the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My setup lives in a single Git repository. One &lt;code&gt;git pull&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;stow */&lt;/code&gt; and any machine is identical to the rest.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Avoid z-index Mess with CSS Isolation</title><link>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/avoid-z-index-mess-with-css-isolation/</link><pubDate>Sun, 14 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/avoid-z-index-mess-with-css-isolation/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;You have a navbar, a modal, and a tooltip inside that modal:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#cad3f5;background-color:#24273a;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-css" data-lang="css"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#eed49f"&gt;navbar&lt;/span&gt; { &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;sticky&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;z-index&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#eed49f"&gt;modal&lt;/span&gt; { &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;fixed&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;z-index&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;50&lt;/span&gt;; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#eed49f"&gt;tooltip&lt;/span&gt; { &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;absolute&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;z-index&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Then someone adds a message alert that floats above the page content:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#cad3f5;background-color:#24273a;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-css" data-lang="css"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;.&lt;span style="color:#eed49f"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt; { &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;position&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;fixed&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;z-index&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#f5a97f"&gt;60&lt;/span&gt;; }
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now the alert bleeds over the modal. You bump the modal to &lt;code&gt;z-index: 80&lt;/code&gt;. But now the tooltip inside it pokes through the navbar. You bump the navbar too. Someone adds a sidebar dropdown that needs to sit above the page but below the modal. You add another value. Eventually the stylesheet is full of &lt;code&gt;999&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;9998&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;10000&lt;/code&gt;, and nobody dares touch them.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Custom Input Component with React Hook Form</title><link>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/custom-input-component-with-react-hook-form/</link><pubDate>Sun, 08 Oct 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://vh-x.github.io/posts/custom-input-component-with-react-hook-form/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Using React Hook Form is a great way to handle inputs without managing state heavily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;a href="https://react-hook-form.com/get-started#Registerfields" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;the official guide&lt;/a&gt; mentioned, you can easily pass the necessary props like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#cad3f5;background-color:#24273a;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-jsx" data-lang="jsx"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; {&lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;...register&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ed8796"&gt;(&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ed8796"&gt;&amp;#34;)&lt;/span&gt;} /&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;However, when you try to make a custom input component that behaves like the native one but with extra functionalities like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#cad3f5;background-color:#24273a;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-jsx" data-lang="jsx"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#6e738d;font-style:italic"&gt;// Takes a &amp;#34;label&amp;#34; prop along with all &amp;lt;input /&amp;gt; props
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; LabeledInput &lt;span style="color:#91d7e3;font-weight:bold"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; ({ label, ...props }) =&amp;gt; (
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; {label}
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; {&lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;...props&lt;/span&gt;} /&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &amp;lt;/&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;);
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;...
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;span style="color:#c6a0f6"&gt;LabeledInput&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#91d7e3;font-weight:bold"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6da95"&gt;&amp;#34;Name&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#91d7e3;font-weight:bold"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6da95"&gt;&amp;#34;Enter your name...&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#8aadf4"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt; /&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;And try to register the input the same way:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title/><link>https://vh-x.github.io/about/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://vh-x.github.io/about/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="about-me"&gt;
 About me
 &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#about-me"&gt;
 &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
 &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hi, I’m a self-taught web developer from Taiwan who’s been into tech and hacking around with code long before I even knew what a “developer” meant. I love figuring out how things work and making them better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I’m all about learning beyond the fundamentals, exploring some low-level stuff, and diving into computer science concepts—not just sticking to the latest trends in tech.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>